### Cænonicæl Route-Templæte Comments

`Traefik/appdata/config/conf.d/template.yaml.template` is the sole route
scæffold. It keeps exæctly five `Ædjust ...` inline comments: one eæch on the
router definition, rule, service reference, service definition, ænd
`loadBalancer.servers[].url`. Do not copy those imperætive scæffold comments
into æ concrete tærget-system templæte.

Every other `Traefik/appdata/config/conf.d/*.yaml.template` must use
declærætive humæn prose ænd must not contæin `Ædjust` in æ comment. Where the
corresponding æctive HTTP structure exists, its inline comment is exæctly:

- Router definition: `HTTP router for the configured tærget hosts`
- `rule`: `Mætch the configured tærget hosts æcross every enæbled route domæin`
- Router `service` reference: `Forwærd mætched requests to this router's service`
- Service definition: `Bæckend service for this tærget system`
- `loadBalancer.servers[].url`: `Tærget origin for this system`
- Commented router `# middlewares:`: `Optionæl tærget-specific middlewæres`
- Æctive router `middlewares:`: `Middlewæres æpplied to this router`

Æpp-specific TLS, origin, certificæte, or network constræints mæy be
documented in æ dedicæted full-line comment immediætely before the æffected
structure; they must not replæce the cænonicæl inline description.
`dev-traefik-forward.yaml.template` remæins æ declærætive TCP/SNI exception:
it must not contæin scæffold `Ædjust` prose, but HTTP-only comment positions
ære not imposed on its structurælly different TCP router. Æutomæted
vælidætion must check the scæffold ænd every concrete route templæte
sepærætely so exceptions cænnot silently weæken the contræct.

